/-!
# Coherent amplitudes and uniform-phase calibration

Complex amplitudes, a positive power-law readout, and independently uniform
phases are explicit model choices. Within this model, mean rate two identifies
exponent two. The expectation is evaluated by a proved Beta/Gamma identity.
The ordered action semantics also interprets exact rational complex amplitudes.

Reference: Skilling and Knuth (2018), §4.3, arXiv:1712.09725.
-/
